WEBVTT

00:55:09.932 --> 00:55:13.685
- Good afternoon, class.
- Good afternoon, madam hooch.

00:55:13.894 --> 00:55:16.688
Good afternoon, Amanda.
Good afternoon.

00:55:17.981 --> 00:55:20.442
Welcome to your first flying lesson.

00:55:20.651 --> 00:55:24.571
What are you waiting for?
Step up to your broomstick.

00:55:24.738 --> 00:55:30.369
Come on now, hurry up. Stick your hand
over the broom and say, "up."

00:55:38.752 --> 00:55:40.379
Up. Up!

00:55:40.587 --> 00:55:42.589
With feeling.

00:55:42.756 --> 00:55:43.841
All: Up!

00:55:48.387 --> 00:55:50.347
Up! Om

00:55:51.265 --> 00:55:53.392
shut up, Harry.

00:55:53.600 --> 00:55:58.272
Now, once you've got hold of
your broom, I want you to mount it.

00:55:58.480 --> 00:56:02.484
Grip it tight. You don't wanna be
sliding off the end.

00:56:02.860 --> 00:56:07.781
When I blow my whistle, I want you
to kick off from the ground, hard.

00:56:08.031 --> 00:56:11.869
Keep your broom steady,
hover for a moment...

00:56:12.077 --> 00:56:16.373
Then lean fonnard slightly
and touch back down.

00:56:16.623 --> 00:56:19.751
On my whistle. Three, two...

00:56:22.129 --> 00:56:23.547
Mr. Longbottom.

00:56:28.135 --> 00:56:31.054
- Mr. Longbottom!
- Down, down!

00:56:31.263 --> 00:56:32.514
Neville!

00:56:36.226 --> 00:56:38.896
Come back down this instant!

00:56:48.822 --> 00:56:51.325
Mr. Longbo...

00:57:00.000 --> 00:57:02.753
Neville: Whoa!

00:57:07.841 --> 00:57:10.260
Madam hooch:
Everyone out of the way!

00:57:15.807 --> 00:57:17.976
Is he all right?

00:57:18.352 --> 00:57:24.024
Oh, dear, it's a broken wrist.
Poor boy. Come on now, up you get.

00:57:25.317 --> 00:57:29.988
Keep your feet on the ground
while I take him to the hospital wing.

00:57:30.197 --> 00:57:33.867
Understand? If I see
a single broom in the air...

00:57:34.076 --> 00:57:39.331
The one riding it will be expelled
before they can say ouidditch.

00:57:39.539 --> 00:57:41.458
Did you see his face?

00:57:41.667 --> 00:57:45.504
If he had squeezed this, he'd have
remembered to fall on his arse.

00:57:45.712 --> 00:57:48.215
Give it here, Malfoy.

00:57:49.049 --> 00:57:52.719
No. I'll leave it somewhere
for Longbottom to find.

00:57:56.890 --> 00:57:59.393
How about on the roof?

00:58:00.560 --> 00:58:04.398
What's the matter, Potter?
Bit beyond your reach?

00:58:06.900 --> 00:58:10.737
Harry, no way!
You heard what madam hooch said.

00:58:10.904 --> 00:58:13.865
Besides, you don't know how to fly.

00:58:19.413 --> 00:58:22.916
Give it here or I'll
knock you off your broom!

00:58:23.166 --> 00:58:25.252
Is that so?

00:58:28.422 --> 00:58:30.716
Have it your way, then.

00:59:03.457 --> 00:59:07.085
Boy 1: Nice going, Harry.
Boy 2: That was wicked, Harry!

00:59:07.294 --> 00:59:09.296
Harry Potter!

00:59:10.297 --> 00:59:12.299
Follow me.

00:59:23.977 --> 00:59:26.229
You wait here.

00:59:27.981 --> 00:59:33.278
Professor quirrell, excuse me.Could I borrow wood for a moment?

00:59:33.487 --> 00:59:35.322
Yes, of course.

00:59:40.994 --> 00:59:46.750
Potter, this is Oliver wood.
Wood, I have found you a seeker.

00:59:48.835 --> 00:59:52.339
Have you heard? Harry Potter's
the new Gryffindor seeker.

00:59:52.589 --> 00:59:54.800
I always knew he'd do well.

00:59:55.258 --> 00:59:59.304
Seeker? But first years
never make the house teams.

00:59:59.513 --> 01:00:04.351
- You must be the youngest player in...
- A century, McGonagall says.

01:00:04.518 --> 01:00:06.853
Well done, Harry.
Wood's just told us.

01:00:07.020 --> 01:00:09.523
Fred and George are on the team.
Beaters.

01:00:09.773 --> 01:00:13.485
Our job is to make sure you
don't get bloodied up too bad.

01:00:13.693 --> 01:00:16.363
Can't make any promises.
Rough game, Quidditch.

01:00:16.530 --> 01:00:20.534
But no one's died in years.
Someone vanishes occasionally.

01:00:20.742 --> 01:00:23.495
But they'll turn up in a month or two.

01:00:23.745 --> 01:00:29.376
Go on. Quidditch is great. Best game
there is, and you'll be great too.

01:00:29.543 --> 01:00:32.796
I've never played.
What if I make a fool of myself?

01:00:33.213 --> 01:00:38.009
You won't make a fool of yourself.
It's in your blood.

01:00:46.560 --> 01:00:50.397
You never told me your father
was a seeker too.

01:00:57.904 --> 01:01:02.534
I'm telling you, it's spooky.
She knows more about you than you do.
